      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but honestly, 'severe hypertensive crisis' sounds really dramatic... it's just some ham. i feel like i'm being way too cautious. i've read online that if you just drink a ton of water and take some ibuprofen, you can flush out any bad reactions or keep the blood pressure stable. wouldn't that work if i accidentally eat something with tyramine? i'd rather just manage it as it happens instead of cutting out everything i love.",
